RDS
Remote desktop Service > It is a Microsoft technology that allows users to remotely access applications and desktop it is commonly used to provide secure remote access to internal resources, enabling users to work from anywhere.
Deployment types:
Session based virtualization: This allows multiple users to share a single server providing a cost effective solution for remote access.
Virtual Desktop Infrastructure: This provides each users with a sep dedicated virtual machine offering a more personalized and high performance experience.
RD Session Host: The remote desktop Session host is a server role that enables multiple users to remotely connect to and run apps or desktops on a single server via the remote desktop protocol RDP.
It is a core component of remote desktop services (RDS) formally known as Terminal Services.
RD Connection Broker > RD Connection Broker role is a server role that acts as the central orchestration and load-balancing computers within remote desktop services (RDS).
It manages user connections, session assignments and also reconnects the disconnected sessions.
RD Web Access: The RD WA is a server role that provides a web-based portal / interface for users to access the published RDS resources.
Administrators publish resources via Remote Desktop Connection Broker. RD Web Access displays them dynamically.
Users login via a browser to view and launch the published resources.
RD Gateway > It is a server role that grants users on public network access to windows desktops and applications hosted on.
RD Gateway > It grants users on public network access to intranet RDS resources (Windows desktop and applications).
It acts as a gateway, tunneling RDP traffic without exposing RDP ports directly to public internet.
OR
The RD Gateway role enables secure, encrypted connections to RDS resources, (desktop/remote apps) over the internet.
Virtualization Host: Remote desktop virtualization host integrates with Hyper-V to host virtual machines and provide them to users as VM.
With RD Gateway, users can access internal network resources from remote locations without the need of a VPN.
RD Licensing > It refers to the role manages remote desktop services, client access licenses also known as CAL's, enabling compliant access to RDS session-based functionality. Such as multi-user desktops and remote app programs hosted on RDSH servers.
This role authenticates incoming connections, issues CALS (with help of DC), tracks usage and enforces licensing policies.
Key functionality:
Issues CAL: Grants per user or per device RDS CALs to validated clients.
Compliance Reporting: Provides usage diagnostics, over-allocation alerts and audit logs.
