CONNECTION FLOW RDS (Without Gateway)
User initiates connection by entering URL (eg: https://rdwa.domain.com/rdweb) The connection happens on port 443 for HTTPS.
Firewall checks if the user should be allowed or not to enter premises. If allowed the request gets to RDWA.
After firewall it gets to RD Web Access. It checks through Internet Information Service (IIS) > Web Access reaches out to AD and asks if the user should be allowed or not. (IIS authenticates it)
IIS authentication is a form based authentication.
Port 5504 creates a tunnel which helps RD Web access to get information about which apps / resource are to be accessed by a particular domain.
